1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:05,682
This is Colorado's oldest scenic byway!

2
00:00:05,682 --> 00:00:08,765
A stone chapel built right on top of a rock.

3
00:00:08,765 --> 00:00:11,917
An old gold camp hanging on the mountainside.

4
00:00:11,917 --> 00:00:15,210
And the gulch where Colorado's gold rush began!

5
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:23,153
This is the Peak to Peak Highway: 55 miles along the Front Range, from Estes Park all the way to Black Hawk.

6
00:00:23,153 --> 00:00:26,520
Stick around till the end for the full trip planner!

7
00:00:27,470 --> 00:00:28,559
Here's the plan!

8
00:00:28,559 --> 00:00:37,610
We leave Estes Park, stop at Chapel on the Rock, climb to the old gold camp of Ward, cruise into Nederland, and finish in Black Hawk!

9
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:40,707
We're starting in Estes Park!

10
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:48,630
Grab a coffee, because today we're driving Colorado's oldest scenic byway, first laid out way back in 1918!

11
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:54,128
South on Highway 7, and look at Longs Peak filling the windshield!

12
00:00:54,128 --> 00:00:59,090
Quick stop at Lily Lake for a flat, easy loop with a huge mountain view.

13
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:08,363
This is Chapel on the Rock, a stone chapel built right on top of a giant boulder, with Mount Meeker towering behind it.

14
00:01:08,363 --> 00:01:12,420
Even Pope John Paul the Second stopped here, back in 1993!

15
00:01:13,370 --> 00:01:16,949
Through tiny Allenspark and deep into aspen country!

16
00:01:16,949 --> 00:01:20,597
Come in late September and whole hillsides turn gold.

17
00:01:20,597 --> 00:01:26,310
And just past Ward, Brainard Lake is one of the prettiest spots in the Front Range!

18
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:35,221
Welcome to Ward, an old gold camp hanging right on the mountainside at nine thousand four hundred fifty feet!

19
00:01:35,221 --> 00:01:37,850
Miners found gold here back in 1860.

20
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:43,527
Now we roll south toward Nederland, with the Indian Peaks behind us.

21
00:01:43,527 --> 00:01:47,280
This whole stretch stays up around nine thousand feet!

22
00:01:48,230 --> 00:01:49,656
Welcome to Nederland!

23
00:01:49,656 --> 00:01:54,002
The name means low lands in Dutch, after a Dutch mining company.

24
00:01:54,002 --> 00:01:58,279
Don't miss the Carousel of Happiness, with hand-carved animals.

25
00:01:58,279 --> 00:01:59,230
It's adorable!

26
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:04,885
Down Highway 119 we go, through Rollinsville and into the canyon.

27
00:02:04,885 --> 00:02:10,530
Get ready, because we're heading to the spot where Colorado's gold rush began!

28
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:13,370
We made it to Black Hawk!

29
00:02:13,370 --> 00:02:19,794
In 1859, John Gregory struck gold right here, and it kicked off Colorado's gold rush.

30
00:02:19,794 --> 00:02:24,480
Today it's a casino town, and Central City is right next door!

31
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:28,118
And that's the Peak to Peak Highway!

32
00:02:28,118 --> 00:02:34,390
55 miles from Estes Park to Black Hawk, through the oldest scenic byway in Colorado.

33
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:38,500
Here's your trip planner, everything in one place.

34
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:40,270
Pause and grab a screenshot!

35
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,349
Thanks for riding along!

36
00:02:45,349 --> 00:02:51,510
Hit subscribe, and next time we're taking I-70 from Denver to the hot springs in Glenwood Springs!
